    id: "crochet-ladybug",
    title: "The Whimsy Folks - Amigurumi Doll Crochet Pattern",
    description: "Crochet a whimsical 15 (or 18 long-limbed) doll in super bulky yarn, worked in the round with legs, body and head in one piece. Make your own Whimsy Folk with a bonnet, ears, antennae or mushrooms, puffy flowers, hair, a belly pocket and felt eye flower patches.",
    patternText: `<h1>Ladybug - Amigurumi Crochet Pattern</h1><p>Crochet a cute 7 cm (2.7 in) ladybug in tight-stitched cotton with a 2.0 mm hook. The pattern covers the belly, back, muzzle, big white eyes, six paws and black spots, with step-by-step assembly. Easy to make in red, orange or any color you like.</p><section><h2>Materials and Tools</h2><ul><li>100% cotton yarn. The designer used PaintBox Yarns Cotton DK (125 m, 50 g): Pillar Red (415), Granite Grey (407), a small amount of Champagne White (403) and Pure Black (402)</li><li>2.0 mm hook (the designer used Clover)</li><li>Stuffing (hollow fiber)</li><li>Black beads, 6 mm in diameter, for eyes</li><li>A needle with a big eye</li><li>Sewing pins</li></ul><p><em>Note: The toy must be crocheted with tight stitches so there are no holes through which the stuffing can be seen. If there are tiny holes, use a smaller hook. The ladybug is approximately 7 cm (2.7 in) if you use the same materials as the designer.</em></p></section><section><h2>Used Stitches</h2><ul><li><b>ch</b> - chain</li><li><b>sc</b> - single crochet</li><li><b>sl st</b> - slip stitch</li><li><b>sc inc</b> - increase</li><li><b>sc dec</b> - decrease</li><li><b>(sc, inc)*n</b> - repeat the stitches in brackets n times</li></ul></section><section><h2>Belly</h2><p>Dark gray yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in a spiral.</p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 6 sc in magic ring (6)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 2 sc in each sc (12)</li><li><strong>Row 3:</strong> (1 sc, sc inc)*6 (18)</li><li><strong>Row 4:</strong> (2 sc, sc inc)*6 (24)</li><li><strong>Row 5:</strong> (3 sc, sc inc)*6 (30)</li><li><strong>Row 6:</strong> (4 sc, sc inc)*6 (36)</li><li><strong>Row 7:</strong> (5 sc, sc inc)*6 (42)</li><li><strong>Row 8:</strong> (6 sc, sc inc)*6 (48)</li><li><strong>Row 9:</strong> (7 sc, sc inc)*6 (54)</li><li><strong>Row 10:</strong> (8 sc, sc inc)*6, sl st (60)</li></ul><p>Tie off the thread and cut it.</p></section><section><h2>Back</h2><p>Red yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in a spiral.</p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 6 sc in magic ring (6)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 2 sc in each sc (12)</li><li><strong>Row 3:</strong> (1 sc, sc inc)*6 (18)</li><li><strong>Row 4:</strong> (2 sc, sc inc)*6 (24)</li><li><strong>Row 5:</strong> (3 sc, sc inc)*6 (30)</li><li><strong>Row 6:</strong> (4 sc, sc inc)*6 (36)</li><li><strong>Row 7:</strong> (5 sc, sc inc)*6 (42)</li><li><strong>Row 8:</strong> 42 sc (42)</li><li><strong>Row 9:</strong> (6 sc, sc inc)*6 (48)</li><li><strong>Row 10:</strong> 48 sc (48)</li><li><strong>Row 11:</strong> (7 sc, sc inc)*6 (54)</li><li><strong>Row 12:</strong> 54 sc (54)</li><li><strong>Row 13:</strong> (8 sc, sc inc)*6 (60)</li><li><strong>Row 14:</strong> 60 sc (60)</li></ul><p>Don't cut the working thread.</p><p><b>Joining the belly and back:</b> put the wrong sides of the pieces against each other, insert the hook through the loops of both pieces and crochet sc. Work sc around the whole edge, stuffing the body as you go. Finish with sl st. Tie off the thread and hide it inside.</p></section><section><h2>Muzzle</h2><p>Dark gray yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in rows. Chain 5.</p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> starting in the second chain from the hook: 1 sc inc, 2 sc, 1 sc inc, 1 ch, turn (6)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 1 sc inc, 4 sc, 1 sc inc, 1 ch, turn (8)</li><li><strong>Rows 3-6:</strong> 4 rows of 8 sc, 1 ch, turn (8)</li><li><strong>Row 7:</strong> 6 sc, 1 sc dec, 1 ch, turn (7)</li><li><strong>Row 8:</strong> 1 sc dec, 5 sc, 1 ch, turn (6)</li><li><strong>Row 9:</strong> 5 sc, 1 sc inc, 1 ch, turn (7)</li><li><strong>Row 10:</strong> 1 sc inc, 6 sc, 1 ch, turn (8)</li><li><strong>Rows 11-14:</strong> 4 rows of 8 sc, 1 ch, turn (8)</li><li><strong>Row 15:</strong> 1 sc dec, 4 sc, 1 sc dec, 1 ch, turn (6)</li><li><strong>Row 16:</strong> 1 sc dec, 2 sc, 1 sc dec, 1 ch (4)</li></ul><p>Don't cut the thread; work sc around the edge of the muzzle. Finish with sl st. Tie off the thread and leave enough for sewing.</p></section><section><h2>Eyes (make 2)</h2><p>White yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in a spiral.</p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 6 sc in magic ring (6)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 2 sc in each sc (12)</li><li><strong>Row 3:</strong> (1 sc, sc inc)*6 (18)</li></ul><p>Finish with sl st. Tie off and leave enough thread for sewing.</p></section><section><h2>Paws (make 6)</h2><p>Dark gray yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in a spiral. Do not stuff.</p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 5 sc in magic ring (5)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 2 sc in each sc (10)</li><li><strong>Rows 3-5:</strong> 3 rows of 10 sc (10)</li></ul><p>Fold the two edges of the paw together and work 4 sc through both. Finish with 1 ch. Tie off the thread and leave enough for sewing.</p></section><section><h2>Spots (as many as you like)</h2><p>Black yarn, 2.0 mm hook. Crochet in a spiral.</p><p><b>Big spot:</b></p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 6 sc in magic ring (6)</li><li><strong>Row 2:</strong> 2 sc in each sc, sl st (12)</li></ul><p>Tie off and leave enough thread for sewing.</p><p><b>Small spot:</b></p><ul><li><strong>Row 1:</strong> 6 sc in magic ring (6)</li></ul><p>Finish with sl st. Tie off and leave enough thread for sewing.</p></section><section><h2>Assembly</h2><ol><li>Crochet a chain of 27 ch with dark gray yarn and sew the chain onto the body (down the middle of the back).</li><li>Sew the muzzle onto the body.</li><li>Sew the two black beads onto the whites of the eyes. If you don't have beads, you can embroider the eyes.</li><li>Sew the whites of the eyes onto the muzzle.</li><li>Sew the paws onto the body.</li><li>Sew the spots onto the back.</li></ol><p>Congratulations! Your ladybug is ready. Happy crocheting!</p></section>`,
