    id: "crochet-pinkBlanket",
    title: "daisy white and pink granny blanket PATTERN",
    description: "Turn a simple daisy granny square into the ultimate cozy aesthetic! 💖 Watch how 100+ handmade squares come together to transform this entire bedroom set.",
    patternText: `<div><h1>Daisy Meadow Granny Square Blanket Pattern</h1><p><strong>Skill Level:</strong> Easy-Intermediate[cite: 115] | <strong>Square Size:</strong> 6 in (15 cm)[cite: 115] | <strong>Hook:</strong> 4.5 mm (US 7)[cite: 115] | <strong>Yarn:</strong> Worsted weight in Blush Pink, White, and Yellow[cite: 115].</p><h2>Abbreviations</h2><ul><li><strong>ch:</strong> Chain[cite: 115]</li><li><strong>sl st:</strong> Slip stitch[cite: 115]</li><li><strong>sc:</strong> Single crochet[cite: 115]</li><li><strong>dc:</strong> Double crochet[cite: 116]</li><li><strong>sc2tog:</strong> Single crochet 2 together[cite: 116]</li><li><strong>MR:</strong> Magic ring[cite: 116]</li><li><strong>sp:</strong> Space[cite: 116]</li><li><strong>st(s):</strong> Stitch(es)[cite: 116]</li><li><strong>Rnd:</strong> Round[cite: 116]</li></ul><h2>The Daisy Square</h2><p>Work every round with the right side facing you and do not turn[cite: 117].</p><h3>Center (Yellow)</h3><ul><li><strong>Rnd 1:</strong> Make a MR. Ch 1, work 6 sc into the ring, pull tail to close, sl st to the first sc. (6 sts)[cite: 117]</li><li><strong>Rnd 2:</strong> Ch 1, 2 sc in each st around, sl st to the first sc. (12 sts)[cite: 117]</li><li><strong>Rnd 3:</strong> Ch 1, [1 sc in next st, 2 sc in next st] around, sl st to the first sc. (18 sts)[cite: 117]</li><li><strong>Rnd 4:</strong> Ch 1, [1 sc in next 2 sts, 2 sc in next st] around, sl st to the first sc. Fasten off yellow. (24 sts)[cite: 117]</li></ul><h3>Petals (White)</h3><ul><li><strong>Rnd 5:</strong> Join white with a sl st in any st. *Ch 4, skip 1 st, sl st in next st; repeat around, ending with last sl st in same st as join. (12 ch-4 loops)[cite: 117]</li><li><strong>Rnd 6:</strong> Work into each ch-4 loop: (sc, dc, dc, sc). Repeat in every loop, sl st to the first sc. Fasten off white. (48 sts)[cite: 117]</li></ul><h3>Pink Ring</h3><ul><li><strong>Rnd 7:</strong> Join pink with a standing sc in first st of any petal, sc in next 3 sts, sc2tog over next 2 sts. *Sc in next 4 sts, sc2tog over next 2 sts; repeat 6 more times, sl st to the first sc. (40 sts)[cite: 117]</li></ul><h3>Granny Rounds (Pink)</h3><ul><li><strong>Rnd 8:</strong> Ch 3, 2 dc in same st, ch 2, 3 dc in same st. *Ch 1, skip 1 st, dc in next 3 sts, ch 1, skip 1 st, dc in next 3 sts, ch 1, skip 1 st, (3 dc, ch 2, 3 dc) in next marked st; repeat 2 more times. Ch 1, skip 1 st, dc in next 3 sts, ch 1, skip 1 st, dc in next 3 sts, ch 1, skip last st, sl st to top of beginning ch 3. (per side: 2 clusters, 3 ch-1 sps)[cite: 118]</li><li><strong>Rnd 9:</strong> Sl st in each of next 2 dc and into ch-2 corner sp. Ch 3, 2 dc in same sp, ch 2, 3 dc in same sp. *[Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 3 times, ch 1, (3 dc, ch 2, 3 dc) in next corner sp; repeat 2 more times. [Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 3 times, ch 1, sl st to top of beginning ch 3. (per side: 3 clusters)[cite: 118]</li><li><strong>Rnd 10:</strong> Sl st to next corner sp as before. Ch 3, 2 dc in same sp, ch 2, 3 dc in same sp. [Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 4 times, ch 1, (3 dc, ch 2, 3 dc) in next corner sp; repeat 2 more times. [Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 4 times, ch 1, sl st to top of beginning ch 3. (per side: 4 clusters)[cite: 118]</li><li><strong>Rnd 11:</strong> Sl st to next corner sp as before. Ch 3, 2 dc in same sp, ch 2, 3 dc in same sp. [Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 5 times, ch 1, (3 dc, ch 2, 3 dc) in next corner sp; repeat 2 more times. [Ch 1, 3 dc in next ch-1 sp] 5 times, ch 1, sl st to top of beginning ch 3. Fasten off. (per side: 5 clusters, 6 ch-1 sps)[cite: 118]</li></ul><h3>Finishing & Joining</h3><ul><li><strong>Finishing:</strong> Weave in all ends. Wet or steam block every square to 6 in (15 cm).[cite: 118]</li><li><strong>Joining:</strong> Join squares into strips first using pink, then join the strips.[cite: 119]</li><li><strong>Border Rnd 1:</strong> Join pink in any corner. Ch 1, sc evenly around blanket, 3 sc in each outer corner, sl st to first sc.[cite: 119]</li><li><strong>Border Rnd 2:</strong> Ch 1, work reverse sc (crab stitch) in each st around, sl st to first st and fasten off.[cite: 119]</li></ul></div>`,
