    title: "Crochet High Top Baby Sneakers Pattern With Laces PATTERN",
    description: "Master making trendy high-top crochet baby sneakers complete with realistic laces and custom leather tags. This comprehensive pattern covers multiple colorways, making it a top choice for handmade baby gifts and footwear projects.",
    patternText: `<h1>Baby High-Top Sneaker Booties</h1><h2>Materials needed</h2><p>Yarn: 2 hanks of yarn in different colors (Main Color / MC and Contrasting Color / CC). Vita cotton Lily, 100% mercerized cotton, 1.75 oz (50 g) / 137 yds (125 m), or alternative yarns like Scheepjes Catona or Schachenmayr Catania.</p><p>Crochet hook: C/2 or D/3 (2.5 mm or 3 mm), or size needed to obtain gauge.</p><p>Notions: Scissors, tapestry needle or smaller crochet hook, shoe laces or satin ribbon (approx. 4 mm cord), measuring tape, and an optional brooch, tag, or button for decoration.</p><h2>Gauge</h2><p>26 dc × 13 rows = 4 inches (10 cm).</p><h2>Sizes &amp; measurements</h2><p>Formatted for sizes: 0 months / 0–3 months / 3–6 months / 6–12 months.</p><p>0 months: approx. 3.15" (8 cm)</p><p>0–3 months: approx. 3.5" (9 cm)</p><p>3–6 months: approx. 3.9" (10 cm)</p><p>6–12 months: approx. 4.3–4.7" (11–12 cm)</p><p>How to read: Instructions are given for all four sizes in the order 0 months / 0–3 months / 3–6 months / 6–12 months.</p><h2>Step 1: Sole</h2><p>Start: With MC, chain 16 / 19 / 22 / 26.</p><p>Rnd 1: 2 dc in the 4th st from the hook, dc in next 11/14/17/21 sts, 6 dc in the last st; continue to work along the opposite side of the chain: dc in next 11/14/17/21 sts, 3 dc in the last st. Finish with a sl st in ch. (34 / 40 / 46 / 54 sts).</p><p>Rnd 2: Ch 1 (counts as 1 sc), sc in the same st, sc in next st, 2 sc in next st, sc in next 4/5/6/7 sts, hdc in next 2 sts, dc in next 5/7/9/12 sts, 2 dc in each of next 6 st, dc in next 5/7/9/12 sts, hdc in next 2 sts, sc in next 4/5/6/7 sts, 2 sc in next st, sc in next st, 2 sc in next st. Finish with sl st in ch. (44 / 50 / 56 / 64 sts).</p><p>Rnd 3: Ch 3 (counts as 1 dc), dc in the same st, [dc in next st, 2 dc in next st] 2 times, dc in next 11/14/17/21 sts, [2 dc in next st, dc in next st] 6 times, dc in next 11/14/17/21 sts, [2 dc in next st, dc in next st] 2 times, 2 dc in next st. Finish with sl st in ch. (56 / 62 / 68 / 76 sts). Fasten off and cut yarn.</p><h2>Step 2: Sidepiece</h2><p>Rnd 1: With CC, work starting from BOR with RS facing you. Work sc by inserting the hook not in the st, but under the post of dc of the previous rnd of the sole (RS is inside the bootie). Ch 1 (counts as sc), sc in next 55/61/67/75 post of dc. Finish with sl st in ch. (56 / 62 / 68 / 76 sts).</p><p>Rnd 2: Ch 3 (counts as dc), dc in next 55/61/67/75 sts. Finish with sl st in ch. (56 / 62 / 68 / 76 sts).</p><p>Rnd 3: Ch 1 (counts as sc), sc in next 55/61/67/75 sts. Finish with sl st in ch. (56 / 62 / 68 / 76 sts). Fasten off and cut yarn.</p><p>Note: If the baby's foot is chubby or has high arches, repeat round 3 for 1–2 more rows.</p><h2>Step 3: Toe</h2><p>Worked back and forth in rows with decreases.</p><p>Row 1 (WS): Count 14 / 15 / 16 / 18 sts starting from the BOR, join CC yarn at the 15th / 16th / 17th / 19th st. Ch 2, dc in next st, dc2tog 13 / 15 / 17 / 19 times.</p><p>Row 2 (RS): Ch 2, dc in next st, dc2tog 6 / 7 / 8 / 9 times.</p><p>Row 3 (WS): Ch 2, dc6tog / dc7tog / dc8tog / dc9tog. Fasten off and cut yarn.</p><h2>Step 4: Bootie Tongue</h2><p>Worked back and forth in rows using CC for all sizes.</p><p>Row 1: Join yarn at the indicated starting stitch. Ch 3 (counts as dc), 6 dc in horizontal sts of the toe, dc in the designated side st, 6 dc in next horizontal sts of the toe, work the last dc in the final designated st. (15 sts). Turn.</p><p>Rows 2–8: Ch 3 (counts as dc), dc in next 14 sts. (15 sts). Turn.</p><p>Finish: Fasten off and cut yarn.</p><h2>Step 5: The Upper Part (High-Top Cuff)</h2><p>Row 1: Join MC at the starting side stitch. Ch 3 (counts as dc), dc in next st, then continue to work dc in next 28 / 30 / 32 / 36 sts, and work dc in the final 2 designated sts. (32 / 34 / 36 / 40 sts). Turn.</p><p>Rows 2–10: Ch 3 (counts as dc), dc in next 31 / 33 / 35 / 39 sts. (32 / 34 / 36 / 40 sts). Turn.</p><p>Finish: Fasten off and cut yarn.</p><h2>Step 6: Finishing</h2><p>Ends: Weave in all ends with a tapestry needle or crochet hook.</p><p>Decorate: Decorate the toe with a tag, brooch, or button if desired.</p><p>Laces: Fold down three rows of the upper cuff and lace up your shoelaces or ribbon. Repeat for the second bootie.</p><p>Your little sneakers are finished!</p>`,
