    id: "crochet-8keychains",
    title: "Ultimate Cute Crochet Keychain Pattern Bundle  8 Easy Amigurumi & Bag Charm",
    description: "Looking for fast, fun, and adorable crochet projects? This ultimate bundle includes 9 step-by-step crochet keychain patterns that make the perfect quick makes, yarn stash-busters, and handmade gifts!",
    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<div><h2>1. Donut Keychain</h2><p><strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy / Beginner[cite: 44]</p><p><strong>Materials:</strong> Sport/Fine Yarn/4-Ply Weight Yarn (Alize Cotton Gold Beige, YarnArt Jeans Brown, and various colors for sprinkles), 3mm crochet hook, stitch marker, tapestry/yarn needle, and polyester fiberfill[cite: 44]</p><p><strong>Abbreviations:</strong> Ch (chain), SI (slip stitch), Sc (single crochet), Inc (increase), BLO (Back Loop Only)[cite: 44]</p><h3>Donut Base</h3><p>Start with beige yarn, leave a long tail of about 15 cm, and make 20 chains[cite: 44].</p><ul><li>Rnd 1: Sc 20 in the chain (20)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 2: (sc, inc) x 10 (30)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 3: (2 sc, inc) x 10 (40)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 4: (3 sc, inc) x 10 (50)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 5: (4 sc, inc) x 10 (60)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 6-8: Sc around, slip stitch, and leave a long tail for sewing[cite: 44]</li></ul><h3>Donut Frosting / Topping</h3><p>Make the same using brown or any color yarn without needing a long tail (slip stitch and cut the yarn)[cite: 44].</p><ul><li>Rnd 1: Sc 20 in the chain (20)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 2: (sc, inc) x 10 (30)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 3: (2 sc, inc) x 10 (40)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 4: (3 sc, inc) x 10 (50)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 5: (4 sc, inc) x 10 (60)[cite: 44]</li><li>Rnd 6-8: Sc around, slip stitch, and cut the yarn[cite: 44]</li></ul><p>Use a yarn needle to attach colorful yarn stitches as sprinkles[cite: 44].</p><h3>Assembly</h3><p>Attach the inner circle of the donut (base and frosting) using the long tail of yarn with 20 slip stitches[cite: 44]. Attach the outside edges by slip stitching the donut base with the frosting (working in the BLO of the frosting/top base) up to 50 stitches, then fill with polyfill[cite: 44]. Finish slip stitching all the way around (60)[cite: 44].</p><hr><h2>2. Heart Keychain</h2><p><strong>Materials:</strong> 30 meters of St. George Tango yarn, 2mm crochet hook, embroidery needle, fiberfill stuffing, stitch marker, and scissors[cite: 45]. Finished heart is 4 cm tall[cite: 45].</p><p><strong>Abbreviations:</strong> Rnd (round), mr (magic ring), sc (single crochet), inc (increase), dec (decrease)[cite: 45].</p><h3>Instructions</h3><p>Make 2 halves and do not cut the yarn when finishing the second half[cite: 45].</p><ul><li>Rnd 1: 6 sc in mr (6)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 2: Inc x 6 (12)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 3: 12 sc (12)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 4: 6 sc on the second half, 12 sc on the first half, 6 sc on the second half (24)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 5: 24 sc (24)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 6: (4 sc, dec) x 4 (20)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 7: 20 sc (20)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 8: (3 sc, dec) x 4 (16)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 9: 16 sc (16)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 10: (2 sc, dec) x 4 (12)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 11: (1 sc, dec) x 4 (8)[cite: 45]</li><li>Rnd 12: (2 sc, dec) x 2 (6)[cite: 45]</li></ul><p>Finish off, leave a long tail (around 25 cm), cut the yarn, and close the hole[cite: 45]. Use an embroidery needle to pull the yarn through the heart to the top between the two halves[cite: 45]. Chain 20 with your crochet hook and finish off between the two halves to form a hanging loop circle[cite: 45].</p><p><strong>get pdf for full pattern</strong></p></div>`,
