    patternText: `<div><h2>Mini Crossbody Bag Crochet Pattern</h2><p><strong>Skill Level:</strong> Advanced beginner[cite: 73]. <strong>Finished Size:</strong> Width 18.5 cm, Height 11 cm, Depth 4 cm[cite: 75].</p><h3>Materials and Tools</h3><ul><li>Original yarn: Sensy 2 mm (100% polypropylene macrame cord, 251 yards)[cite: 74].</li><li>Hook: 3.50 mm[cite: 74].</li><li>Notions: D-rings, swivel clasp, and bag lock[cite: 74].</li></ul><h3>Step 1. Main Part</h3><p>Leave a long tail of approx 25 cm and make a foundation chain of 31 stitches[cite: 77]. Row 1: 30 sc, 1 ch, turn[cite: 77]. Row 2: Lay the long tail on top and crochet it into the second row, working sc into the back loop of the current row and foundation chain loop (30 sc, 1 ch, turn)[cite: 78].</p><strong>get pdf for full pattern</strong></div>`,
