    title: "Crochet Gnome Keychain Pattern Ruffled Hat Amigurumi Bag Charm",
    description: "Crochet this adorable miniature gnome keychain with a ruffled hat and sweet bobble nose! Perfect for a quick stash-busting project, festive bag charm, or handmade holiday gift. Grab your yarn and hook to stitch this cute pocket gnome today!   ",
    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<div><h3>Ruffled Hat Gnome Keychain Pattern</h3><p><strong>Materials &amp; Tools:</strong> Alize Cotton Gold yarn in light beige and green[cite: 35], Hollowfiber or synthetic stuffing[cite: 35], Keyring with a lobster clasp[cite: 35], 3-4 mm buttons or beads[cite: 35], 6 mm bell[cite: 35], Blush or dry pastel[cite: 35], 2.25 mm crochet hook[cite: 35], Thin sewing needle and wide-eye needle[cite: 35]. <strong>Body &amp; Head:</strong> Worked as a single piece starting from the base with light beige yarn[cite: 35]. Rnd 1: 6 single crochets in a magic ring[cite: 35]. Rnd 2: 6 increases [12][cite: 35]. Rnd 3: (1 single crochet, increase) x 6 [18][cite: 35]. Rnd 4: 1 single crochet, increase, (2 single crochets, increase) x 5, 1 single crochet [24][cite: 35]. Rnd 5: (3 single crochets, increase) x 6 [30][cite: 35]. Rnd 6: 2 single crochets, increase, (4 single crochets, increase) x 5, 2 single crochets [36][cite: 35]. Rnds 7-9: 36 single crochets (3 rows)[cite: 35]. Rnd 10: 17 single crochets, bobble (nose), 18 single crochets [35]. (Adjust the bobble so it pops outward, and stuff the piece as you go.) Switch to green yarn[cite: 35]. Rnd 11: 36 single crochets[cite: 35]. Rnd 12: Working in back loops only: 5 single crochets, decrease, (10 single crochets, decrease) x 2, 5 single crochets [33][cite: 35]. Rnds 13-14: 33 single crochets (2 rows)[cite: 35]. Rnd 15: (9 single crochets, decrease) x 3 [30][cite: 36]. Rnd 16: Working in back loops only: 30 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 17: 30 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 18: 4 single crochets, decrease, (8 single crochets, decrease) x 2, 4 single crochets [27][cite: 36]. Rnd 19: 27 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 20: Working in back loops only: 27 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 21: (7 single crochets, decrease) x 3 [24][cite: 36]. Rnds 22-23: 24 single crochets (2 rows)[cite: 36]. Rnd 24: Working in back loops only: 1 single crochet, decrease, (2 single crochets, decrease) x 5, 1 single crochet [18][cite: 36]. Rnds 25-26: 18 single crochets (2 rows)[cite: 36]. Rnd 27: (1 single crochet, decrease) x 6 [12][cite: 36]. Rnds 28-29: 12 single crochets (2 rows)[cite: 36]. Rnd 30: 6 decreases [6][cite: 36]. Rnds 31-33: 2 single crochets, decrease, 1 single crochet, increase [6] (3 rows)[cite: 36]. Rnd 34: 6 single crochets[cite: 36]. Cut yarn, pull remaining stitches closed, and hide the tail inside[cite: 36]. <strong>Hat Ruffles / Front Loop Trims:</strong> Attach green yarn to the unused front loops of rounds 11, 15, 19, and 23[cite: 36]. Rnd 12 (in front loops of Rnd 11): 36 half double crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 16 (in front loops of Rnd 15): 33 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 20 (in front loops of Rnd 19): 27 single crochets[cite: 36]. Rnd 24 (in front loops of Rnd 23): 24 single crochets[cite: 36]. Fasten off and secure all ends inside[cite: 36].</p></div>`,
