    patternText: `<div><h3>Long-Legged Christmas Gnome Keychain Pattern</h3><p><strong>Specifications &amp; Materials:</strong> Dimensions: ~10 cm tall without legs (22 cm with legs)[cite: 37], Hook size: 2.5 mm or 2 mm[cite: 37], Hollowfiber stuffing[cite: 37], Nako Bambino yarn (25% wool, 75% acrylic, 130 m / 50 g) in white, a bright color, and a bit of pink[cite: 37], Thin black yarn or embroidery floss for facial features[cite: 37], Black beads (d=4-6 mm) for eyes[cite: 37], Plastic or linoleum cutout for the flat base[cite: 37]. <strong>Head-Body:</strong> Start with the bright color yarn[cite: 37]. Rnd 1: 6 single crochets in a magic ring[cite: 37]. Rnd 2: 6 increases = 12 single crochets[cite: 37]. Rnd 3: (increase, 1 single crochet) x 6 = 18 single crochets[cite: 37]. Rnd 4: (2 single crochets, increase) x 6 = 24 single crochets[cite: 37]. Rnd 5: (increase, 3 single crochets) x 6 = 30 single crochets[cite: 37]. Rnd 6: 30 single crochets worked through the back loop only[cite: 37]. Rnds 7-8: 30 single crochets[cite: 37]. Switch to white yarn on the last stitch of round 8[cite: 37]. Rnds 9-12: 30 single crochets worked using loop stitches for the beard[cite: 37]. Insert the cut circular base at the bottom[cite: 37]. <strong>Eye Shaping Rows:</strong> Worked back and forth with a turning chain at the end of each row[cite: 37]. Row 13: 7 single crochets[cite: 37]. Row 14: 6 single crochets[cite: 37]. Row 15: 5 single crochets[cite: 37]. Row 16: 4 single crochets[cite: 37]. Row 17: 3 single crochets[cite: 37]. Fasten off and edge with white single crochets[cite: 37]. <strong>Hat:</strong> Rnd 1: 6 single crochets in a magic ring[cite: 38]. Rnd 2: 6 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 3: Increase, 5 single crochets = 7 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 4: 7 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 5: 4 single crochets, increase, 2 single crochets = 8 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 6: 8 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 7: Increase, 7 single crochets = 9 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 8: 9 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 9: 5 single crochets, increase, 3 single crochets = 10 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 10: 10 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 11: 3 single crochets, increase, 6 single crochets = 11 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 12: 9 single crochets, increase, 1 single crochet = 12 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 13: Increase, 11 single crochets = 13 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 14: 7 single crochets, increase, 5 single crochets = 14 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 15: (4 single crochets, increase, 2 single crochets) x 2 = 16 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 16: (increase, 7 single crochets) x 2 = 18 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 17: (5 single crochets, increase, 3 single crochets) x 2 = 20 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 18: (increase, 9 single crochets) x 2 = 22 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 19: (6 single crochets, increase, 4 single crochets) x 2 = 24 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 20: (increase, 7 single crochets) x 3 = 27 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 21: (5 single crochets, increase, 3 single crochets) x 3 = 30 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 22: (increase, 9 single crochets) x 3 = 33 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 23: 33 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 24: Join the hat to the body by working a row of single crochets through both layers together, stuffing fully before closing[cite: 38]. <strong>Nose (Pink):</strong> Rnd 1: 6 single crochets in a magic ring[cite: 38]. Rnd 2: (increase, 1 single crochet) x 3 = 9 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 3: 9 single crochets[cite: 38]. Rnd 4: (decrease, 1 single crochet) x 3 = 6 single crochets[cite: 38]. Fasten off, leave a tail for sewing, stuff lightly, and attach right against the beard[cite: 38]. <strong>Legs (Make 2):</strong> Start with the bright color yarn[cite: 38]. Chain 6[cite: 38]. Rnd 1: Starting from the 2nd chain from hook: 4 single crochets, 3 single crochets in the end chain[cite: 38]. Working along the opposite side: 3 single crochets, 2 single crochets in the starting chain = 12 single crochets[cite: 38, 39]. Rnd 2: Increase, 3 single crochets, 3 increases, 3 single crochets, 2 increases = 18 single crochets[cite: 39]. Rnd 3: 18 single crochets[cite: 39]. Rnd 4: Make 5 consecutive half double crochet decreases across the front = 13[cite: 39]. Rnd 5: Make 5 consecutive half double crochet decreases across the front = 8[cite: 39]. Stuff the shoe firmly. Do not stuff the rest of the leg[cite: 39]. Alternate colors every 2 rows (white, then bright color) for 8 single crochets per row up to row 33[cite: 39]. Fasten off and sew to the bottom front edge of the body[cite: 39].</p></div>`,
