    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<h2>Materials &amp; Tools</h2><ul><li>Super bulky / super chunky / 14-ply velvet yarn (Himalaya Dolphin Baby) – 2 skeins in different colors</li><li>Sport weight / 4-ply yarn (YarnArt Jeans or Alize Cotton Gold) in black</li><li>30 cm thread for face decoration</li><li>Sewing needle</li><li>Hooks: 3.75 mm and 5 mm</li><li>Wooden button</li><li>Safety eyes, 8–10 mm</li><li>Safety nose, 10 mm</li><li>Stuffing material</li></ul><h2>Notes &amp; Dimensions</h2><ul><li><strong>Size:</strong> 21 cm wide (8.2") and 24 cm high (9.4")</li><li>Work in continuous rounds, in rows, and in a spiral.</li><li>At the beginning of the round, use a marker or thread of a different color to track the beginning of the round.</li></ul><h2>Abbreviations</h2><ul><li><strong>ch:</strong> chain</li><li><strong>MR:</strong> magic ring</li><li><strong>sc:</strong> single crochet</li><li><strong>inc:</strong> increase</li><li><strong>dec:</strong> decrease</li><li><strong>sl st:</strong> slip stitch</li><li><strong>BLO:</strong> back loops only</li><li><strong>t-ch:</strong> turning chain</li><li><strong>hdc:</strong> half double crochet stitch</li><li><strong>hdcinc:</strong> half double crochet increase (2 hdc in one stitch)</li><li><strong>hdc2tog:</strong> crochet 2 hdc together</li><li><strong>(...) * n:</strong> repeat instruction in brackets n times</li><li><strong>(...):</strong> number of loops in a row / round</li></ul><h2>Flap</h2><p>Crochet with pink yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 5 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook. Do not pull the ring. Turn (5).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> t-ch, 1 sc, inc * 4, turn (9).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> t-ch, (sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (13).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> t-ch, (2 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (17).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> t-ch, (3 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (21).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> t-ch, (4 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (25).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> t-ch, (5 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (29).</li><li><strong>8)</strong> t-ch, (7 sc, inc) * 3, 5 sc, turn (32).</li><li><strong>9)</strong> t-ch, (8 sc, inc) * 3, 5 sc (35).</li></ul><p><em>Do not turn. Work along the top of the flap:</em></p><ul><li><strong>10)</strong> t-ch, 19 sc, turn (19).</li><li><strong>11–15)</strong> t-ch, 19 sc, turn (5 rows).</li><li><strong>16)</strong> t-ch, 19 sc (19). Do not turn.</li></ul><p><em>Change color to purple and cut the pink yarn. Work in rounds:</em></p><ul><li><strong>17)</strong> t-ch, 22 sc, 3 ch, skip 3 stitches, 22 sc, turn (47).</li><li><strong>18)</strong> t-ch, 47 reverse sc (47), sl st.</li></ul><h2>Backpack</h2><p>Begin to crochet with purple yarn. Ch 20. Start on the second chain from the hook:</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> 18 sc, 3 sc in the last chain, on the other side of the chain: 17 sc, inc, inc into t-ch (42). Place a marker.</li><li><strong>2)</strong> 16 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 2, inc, 15 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 3 (48).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> inc, 15 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 4, inc, 14 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 4, 1 sc (58).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> inc, 15 sc, (inc, 3 sc) * 3, inc, 17 sc, (inc, 3 sc) * 3 (66).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> inc, 18 sc, (inc, 4 sc) * 3, inc, 16 sc, (inc, 4 sc) * 3 (74).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> 74 sc (74).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> BLO 74 sc (74).</li><li><strong>8–16)</strong> 74 sc (9 rounds).</li><li><strong>17)</strong> 26 sc, dec, 34 sc, dec, 10 sc (72).</li></ul><p><em>Change color to pink and cut the purple yarn.</em></p><ul><li><strong>18–35)</strong> 72 sc (18 rounds).</li></ul><p><em>Join the flap in the next rounds:</em></p><ul><li><strong>36)</strong> 71 sc, 1 sc with the flap (72).</li><li><strong>37)</strong> 20 sc with the flap, 52 sc (72), sl st.</li></ul><h2>Straps</h2><p>Crochet with purple yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 71, start from the second chain on the hook: 70 sc, turn (70).</li><li><strong>2–4)</strong> t-ch, 70 sc (3 rows). (Straps are 50 cm long.)</li></ul><p>Cut the yarn leaving an end for sewing. Sew the straps at the bottom of the backpack between rounds 7 and 11, and at the top between rounds 32 and 36, keeping a distance of 12 sc between them.</p><h2>Handle</h2><p>Crochet with purple yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 21, start from the second chain on the hook: 20 sc, turn (20).</li><li><strong>2–3)</strong> t-ch, 20 sc (20 rows).</li></ul><p>Cut yarn leaving an end for sewing, then sew on the handle.</p><h2>Cord</h2><p>Ch 150. Step back at the top of the backpack 2 rounds and stretch the cord between the stitches after folding the backpack, then make knots at the ends. Sew a button between rounds 23 and 27.</p><h2>Bunny Head</h2><p>Crochet with milk yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 6 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (1 sc, inc) * 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> 1 sc, inc, (2 sc, inc) * 5, 1 sc (24).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> (3 sc, inc) * 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> (4 sc, inc) * 6 (36).</li><li><strong>7–10)</strong> 36 sc (4 rounds).</li><li><strong>11)</strong> (4 sc, dec) * 6 (30).</li><li><strong>12)</strong> (3 sc, dec) * 3 (24).</li></ul><p>Cut yarn leaving an end for sewing. Insert safety eyes between rounds 4 and 5 with a distance of 6–7 sc between them. Insert the safety nose into the middle of the MR, embroider the mouth with pink thread, stuff the head, and sew it to the flap of the backpack.</p><h2>Ears (Make 2)</h2><p>Crochet with milk yarn using a 5 mm hook.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 6 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> hdcinc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (hdc, hdcinc) * 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> (5 hdc, hdcinc) * 3 (21).</li><li><strong>5–6)</strong> 21 hdc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> (5 hdc, hdc2tog) * 3 (18).</li><li><strong>8)</strong> 18 hdc (18).</li><li><strong>9)</strong> (4 hdc, hdc2tog) * 3 (15).</li><li><strong>10–11)</strong> 15 hdc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>12)</strong> (3 hdc, hdc2tog) * 3 (12).</li><li><strong>13–14)</strong> 12 hdc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>15)</strong> (2 hdc, hdc2tog) * 3 (9).</li><li><strong>16–17)</strong> 9 hdc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>18)</strong> 9 sc (9).</li></ul><p>Fold it in half and crochet 4 sc through both sides. Leave an end for sewing, sew on the ears, and embroider lashes with a black cotton thread.</p>`,
