    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<h2>Materials &amp; Tools</h2><ul><li>Super bulky / super chunky / 14-ply velvet yarn (Himalaya Dolphin Baby) – 2 skeins of green, 1/5 skein of cream, and some pink yarn for the cheeks</li><li>Sewing needle</li><li>Hook size 3.75 mm</li><li>Wooden button (2 mm)</li><li>Safety eyes (14 mm)</li><li>Toy stuffing material</li></ul><h2>Notes &amp; Dimensions</h2><ul><li><strong>Size:</strong> 21 cm wide (8.2") and 24 cm high (9.4")</li><li>Work in continuous rounds, in rows, and in a spiral.</li><li>At the beginning of the round, use a marker or thread of a different color to track the beginning of the round.</li></ul><h2>Abbreviations</h2><ul><li><strong>ch:</strong> chain</li><li><strong>MR:</strong> magic ring</li><li><strong>sc:</strong> single crochet</li><li><strong>inc:</strong> increase</li><li><strong>dec:</strong> decrease</li><li><strong>sl st:</strong> slip stitch</li><li><strong>BLO:</strong> back loops only</li><li><strong>t-ch:</strong> turning chain</li><li><strong>(...) * n:</strong> repeat instruction in brackets n times</li><li><strong>(...):</strong> number of loops in a row / round</li></ul><h2>Flap</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 5 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook. Do not pull the ring. Turn (5).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> t-ch, 1 sc, inc * 4, turn (9).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> t-ch, (sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (13).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> t-ch, (2 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (17).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> t-ch, (3 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (21).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> t-ch, (4 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (25).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> t-ch, (5 sc, inc) * 4, 1 sc, turn (29).</li><li><strong>8)</strong> t-ch, (7 sc, inc) * 3, 5 sc, turn (32).</li><li><strong>9)</strong> t-ch, (8 sc, inc) * 3, 5 sc, turn (35).</li><li><strong>10)</strong> t-ch, (9 sc, inc) * 3, 5 sc (38).</li></ul><p><em>Do not turn. Work along the top of the flap:</em></p><ul><li><strong>11)</strong> t-ch, 21 sc, turn (21).</li><li><strong>12–18)</strong> t-ch, 21 sc, turn (6 rows).</li><li><strong>19)</strong> t-ch, 21 sc (21). Do not turn.</li></ul><p><em>Then work in rounds:</em></p><ul><li><strong>20)</strong> t-ch, 26 sc, 3 ch, skip 3 stitches, 25 sc, turn (54).</li><li><strong>21)</strong> t-ch, 53 reverse sc (53), sl st.</li></ul><h2>Backpack Body</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn. Ch 20. Start on the second chain from the hook:</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> 18 sc, 3 sc in the last chain, on the other side of the chain: 17 sc, inc, inc into t-ch (42). Place a marker.</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc, 15 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 2, inc, 17 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 2 (48).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> inc, 1 sc, inc, 15 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 4, inc, 15 sc, (inc, 1 sc) * 3 (58).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> inc, 1 sc, inc, 16 sc, (inc, 3 sc) * 3, inc, 18 sc, (inc, 3 sc) * 2 (66).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> inc, 3 sc, inc, 18 sc, (inc, 4 sc) * 3, inc, 17 sc, (inc, 4 sc) * 2 (74).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> 74 sc (74).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> BLO 74 sc (74).</li><li><strong>8–16)</strong> 74 sc (9 rounds).</li><li><strong>17)</strong> 32 sc, dec, 35 sc, dec, 3 sc (72).</li><li><strong>18–36)</strong> 72 sc (19 rounds).</li></ul><p><em>Join the flap in the next round:</em></p><ul><li><strong>37)</strong> 1 sc, 23 sc with the flap, 48 sc (72), sl st.</li></ul><h2>Straps (Two Pieces)</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 71, start from the second chain on the hook: 70 sc, turn (70).</li><li><strong>2–4)</strong> t-ch, 70 sc (3 rows). (Straps are 50 cm long.)</li></ul><p>Cut the yarn leaving an end for sewing. Sew the straps at the bottom of the backpack between rounds 7 and 11, and at the top between rounds 32 and 36, keeping a distance of 12 sc between them.</p><h2>Handle</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn, working in rows.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 21, start from the second chain on the hook: 20 sc, turn (20).</li><li><strong>2–3)</strong> t-ch, 20 sc (20 rows).</li></ul><p>Cut yarn leaving an end for sewing, then sew on the handle.</p><h2>Cord</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn. Ch 150. Step back at the top of the backpack 2 rounds and stretch the cord between the stitches after folding the backpack, then make knots at the ends. Sew a button between rounds 23 and 27.</p><h2>Frog Head</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 6 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (1 sc, inc) * 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> 1 sc, inc, (2 sc, inc) * 5, 1 sc (24).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> (3 sc, inc) * 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> 2 sc, inc, (4 sc, inc) * 5, 2 sc (36).</li><li><strong>7–10)</strong> 36 sc (4 rounds).</li><li><strong>8)</strong> 2 sc, dec, (4 sc, dec) * 5, 2 sc (30).</li><li><strong>9)</strong> (3 sc, dec) * 6 (24). Stuff the head and leave an end for sewing.</li></ul><h2>Eyes (Make 2)</h2><p>Crochet with cream yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> 6 sc in MR (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li></ul><p><em>Change color to green and cut cream yarn.</em></p><ul><li><strong>3)</strong> (3 sc, inc) * 3 (15). Insert safety eye into the middle of the MR.</li><li><strong>4)</strong> BLO 15 sc (15).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> 15 sc (15).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> (3 sc, dec) * 3 (12). Stuff the eye.</li><li><strong>7)</strong> dec * 6 (6).</li></ul><p>Cut yarn, tighten hole, and weave ends. Attach green yarn to front loops of round 4 and work 15 sl st, leaving a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Tummy</h2><p>Crochet with cream yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> 6 sc in MR (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (sc, inc) * 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4)</strong> 1 sc, inc, (2 sc, inc) * 5, 1 sc (24).</li><li><strong>5)</strong> (3 sc, inc) * 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> 2 sc, inc, (4 sc, inc) * 5, 2 sc, sl st (36).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> (5 sc, inc) * 6 (42).</li><li><strong>8)</strong> 3 sc, inc, (6 sc, inc) * 5, 3 sc (48).</li><li><strong>9)</strong> (7 sc, inc) * 6 (54), sl st. Cut yarn, leaving a tail for sewing.</li></ul><h2>Forelegs (Make 2)</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 6 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (3 sc, inc) * 3 (15).</li><li><strong>4–5)</strong> 15 sc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> (3 sc, dec) * 3 (12).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> (2 sc, dec) * 3 (9). Stuff the lower foreleg.</li><li><strong>8–12)</strong> 9 sc (5 rounds). Fold in half and crochet 4 sc through both sides. Cut yarn leaving a tail for sewing.</li></ul><h2>Hind Legs (Make 2)</h2><p>Crochet with green yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1)</strong> ch 2, crochet 6 sc into the 2nd ch from the hook (6).</li><li><strong>2)</strong> inc * 6 (12).</li><li><strong>3)</strong> (2 sc, inc) * 4 (16).</li><li><strong>4–5)</strong> 16 sc (2 rounds).</li><li><strong>6)</strong> (2 sc, dec) * 4 (12).</li><li><strong>7)</strong> (2 sc, dec) * 3 (9). Stuff the lower leg.</li><li><strong>8–13)</strong> 9 sc (6 rounds). Fold in half and crochet 4 sc through both sides. Cut yarn leaving a tail for sewing.</li></ul><h2>Assembly</h2><ul><li>Sew the eyes between rounds 6 and 10 of the head at a distance of 5 sc.</li><li><strong>Mouth:</strong> Attach green yarn to the stitch between rounds 6 and 7, work 11 sc between the rounds, and sl st. Cut yarn and weave in ends.</li><li>Using pink chenille thread, embroider the cheeks between rounds 3 and 7.</li><li>Sew the head to the flap of the backpack.</li><li>Sew the tummy to the backpack.</li><li>Sew the forelegs between rounds 25 and 28.</li><li>Sew the hind legs between rounds 8 and 12.</li></ul>`,
