    id: "santa-claus",
    title: "Santa Claus Crochet Pattern Plush Amigurumi Christmas Santa with Beard & Hat",
    description: "Crochet a jolly Santa Claus about 35 cm tall, with a fluffy white beard and mustache, a cozy blue velvet coat, a belt and a little hat. He makes a charming Christmas decoration or handmade gift.",
    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<h2>Materials &amp; Tools</h2><ul><li><strong>Finished toy size:</strong> about 35 cm</li><li>Himalaya Dolphin Baby yarn (beige, black)</li><li>Alize Velluto yarn (blue)</li><li>White faux fur / fluffy yarn</li><li>Crochet hook size 4</li><li>Safety eyes (diameter 10–12 mm)</li><li>Plastic sewing needle</li><li>Stitch marker</li><li>Stuffing (holofiber, synthetic fluff)</li></ul><h2>Abbreviations &amp; Terms</h2><ul><li><strong>MR:</strong> magic ring</li><li><strong>CH:</strong> chain</li><li><strong>SC:</strong> single crochet</li><li><strong>SL ST:</strong> slip stitch</li><li><strong>HDC:</strong> half double crochet</li><li><strong>DC:</strong> double crochet</li><li><strong>Inc:</strong> increase</li><li><strong>Dec:</strong> decrease</li></ul><h2>Head</h2><p>Work with beige yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> 1 SC, inc, (2 SC, inc) x 5, 1 SC (24).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> 2 SC, inc, (4 SC, inc) x 5, 2 SC (36).</li><li><strong>7–12.</strong> 36 SC. (Insert safety eyes between rows 9 and 10, with a distance of 5 SC between them.)</li><li><strong>13.</strong> 2 SC, dec, (4 SC, dec) x 5, 2 SC (30).</li><li><strong>14.</strong> (3 SC, dec) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>15.</strong> 1 SC, dec, (2 SC, dec) x 5, 1 SC (18).</li><li><strong>16.</strong> (1 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li></ul><p>Stuff the head, leave a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Nose</h2><p>Work with beige yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li></ul><p>Pull the hole closed. Stuff lightly. Secure and cut the thread, leaving a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Arms (Make 2)</h2><p>Work with beige yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> 12 SC.</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (2 SC, dec) x 3 (9).</li></ul><p><em>Switch to blue yarn.</em></p><ul><li><strong>5.</strong> Work through the back loops only: 9 SC.</li><li><strong>6–8.</strong> 9 SC.</li><li><strong>9.</strong> 7 SC, dec (8).</li><li><strong>10–12.</strong> 8 SC.</li></ul><p>Stuff the lower part. Flatten the piece and crochet 4 SC across both layers together. Secure and cut the thread, leaving a tail for sewing.</p><p>Attach white fluffy yarn to row 5 and crochet 2 rows of SC (9).</p><h2>Legs &amp; Body</h2><p>First, crochet 2 legs. Work with black yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> 18 SC.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> 4 SC, 5 dec, 4 SC (13).</li><li><strong>6–8.</strong> 13 SC.</li></ul><p><em>Switch to beige yarn.</em></p><ul><li><strong>9.</strong> Work in back loops only: 13 SC.</li><li><strong>10.</strong> 13 SC.</li></ul><p><em>Switch to blue yarn.</em></p><ul><li><strong>11.</strong> 13 SC.</li></ul><p>On the first leg, secure and cut the thread. On the second leg, crochet 2 more SC (adjust so it aligns straight) and continue into the body:</p><ul><li><strong>12.</strong> 2 CH, join to the first leg, 13 SC around the first leg, 2 SC along the chain, 13 SC around the second leg, 2 SC along the chain (30).</li><li><strong>13–16.</strong> 30 SC.</li><li><strong>17.</strong> (3 SC, dec) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>18.</strong> Work in back loops only: 24 SC.</li><li><strong>19–20.</strong> 24 SC.</li><li><strong>21.</strong> (2 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>22–23.</strong> 18 SC.</li></ul><p>Stuff tightly.</p><ul><li><strong>24.</strong> (1 SC, dec) x 6 (12).</li><li><strong>25.</strong> 6 dec (6).</li></ul><p>Secure, cut the thread, and pull the hole closed.</p><h2>Coat</h2><p>Attach blue yarn to row 18 (front loops left from round 18), make 2 CH, and crochet a DC in each stitch (24 DC). Crochet 3 rows of 24 DC.</p><p><strong>Edging:</strong> Border the bottom edge with white fluffy yarn – 2 rows of SC (24). Secure and cut the thread.</p><h2>Belt</h2><p>Work with blue yarn. Chain 81, then crochet 80 SC along the chain. Secure and cut the thread.</p><h2>Hat</h2><p>Work with blue yarn.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12 SC).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (inc, SC) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (2 inc, SC) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (3 inc, SC) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> (4 inc, SC) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>7.</strong> (inc, 11 SC) x 3 (39).</li><li><strong>8–9.</strong> 39 SC.</li></ul><p>Secure and cut the thread.</p><p><em>Switch to white fluffy yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>10–12.</strong> 39 SC.</li></ul><p>Secure and cut the thread.</p><p><strong>Trim:</strong> Crochet a row of SL ST with white fluffy yarn along row 9 of the hat. Secure and cut the thread.</p><h2>Beard</h2><p>Work with white fluffy yarn from bottom to top. Chain 2 and crochet in turning rows to the desired length, making an increase in the very last stitch of each row. (Total of 12 rows achieved.) Secure and cut the thread, leaving a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Mustache (Make 2)</h2><p>Work with white fluffy yarn using the same technique as the beard. Secure and cut the thread, leaving a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Assembly &amp; Finishing</h2><ul><li>Embroider eyebrows and eyelashes.</li><li>Sew the nose to the head.</li><li>Sew the head to the body.</li><li>Sew the arms to the body.</li><li>Crochet a vertical line of SC down the front of the coat using white fluffy yarn from the head down to the bottom.</li><li>Place the hat on the head.</li><li>Wrap and secure the belt around the coat.</li><li>Sew the beard to the head.</li><li>Glue or sew on the mustache.</li></ul>`,
