    patternText: `<h2>Materials</h2><ul><li>Yarn (any brand, 50 g = 160–170 m) – green for the body (18 g)</li><li>Dark green thread for facial detailing</li><li>Alize Cotton Gold yarn No. 56 – 10 g</li><li>Fluffy yarn for edging (Softy, Nako Lily) – 2–3 g</li><li>Pom-pom</li><li>2 mm crochet hook</li><li>Needles</li><li>Holofiber stuffing</li><li>Scissors</li><li>12 mm safety eyes with highlights (or simple black eyes)</li><li>15 mm felt circles</li></ul><h2>Head</h2><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in magic ring.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>7–8.</strong> 36 SC each.</li><li><strong>9.</strong> (5 SC, inc) x 6 (42).</li><li><strong>10–11.</strong> 42 SC each.</li><li><strong>12.</strong> (6 SC, inc) x 6 (48).</li><li><strong>13.</strong> 20 SC, 1 ch, skip 1 st, 5 SC, 1 ch, skip 1 st, 21 SC (48).</li><li><strong>14.</strong> (7 SC, inc) x 6 (54).</li><li><strong>15.</strong> 54 SC.</li><li><strong>16.</strong> (3 SC, inc, 4 SC, inc) x 6 (66).</li><li><strong>17–18.</strong> 66 SC each.</li></ul><p>Insert the safety eyes into the felt circles, then insert them into the holes in row 13.</p><ul><li><strong>19.</strong> (9 SC, dec) x 6 (60).</li><li><strong>20.</strong> (8 SC, dec) x 6 (54).</li><li><strong>21.</strong> (2 SC, dec, 3 SC, dec) x 6 (42).</li><li><strong>22.</strong> (5 SC, dec) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>23.</strong> (4 SC, dec) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>24.</strong> (3 SC, dec) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>25.</strong> (2 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li></ul><p>Fasten off and leave a tail for sewing.</p><h2>Arms (Make 2)</h2><p>Start with the body color.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in magic ring.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 3 (9).</li><li><strong>3–4.</strong> 9 SC each.</li></ul><p><em>Switch to the sweater color.</em></p><ul><li><strong>5.</strong> 9 SC.</li><li><strong>6.</strong> Back loops only: 9 SC.</li><li><strong>7–13.</strong> 9 SC each (9 rows).</li></ul><p>Stuff only the lower part where the body color is. Flatten in half and crochet 4 SC through both sides.</p><p>Work an edging with white fluffy yarn in row 6 into the remaining loops (1 SC in each stitch).</p><h2>Legs (Make 2)</h2><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in magic ring.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 SC.</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 3 (9).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> 9 SC.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 3 (12).</li><li><strong>6–7.</strong> 12 SC each.</li></ul><p>On the first leg, fasten off and cut the thread. On the second leg, do not cut the thread, as you will continue directly into the body.</p><h2>Body</h2><p>Connect the legs with 1 chain and continue.</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 12 SC along the first leg, inc (from 3 sts), 12 SC along the second leg, inc (from 3 sts) (30).</li><li><strong>2.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>3–5.</strong> 36 SC each.</li><li><strong>6.</strong> (5 SC, inc) x 6 (42).</li></ul><p><em>Switch from body color to sweater color.</em></p><ul><li><strong>7.</strong> 42 SC.</li><li><strong>8.</strong> Back loops only: 42 SC.</li><li><strong>9–10.</strong> 42 SC each.</li><li><strong>11.</strong> (5 SC, dec) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>12.</strong> 36 SC.</li><li><strong>13.</strong> (4 SC, dec) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>14.</strong> 30 SC.</li><li><strong>15.</strong> (3 SC, dec) x 6 (24). In row 15, make a shift stitch so the marker sits in the middle of the back.</li><li><strong>16.</strong> Crochet the arms in: 4 SC, 4 SC together with the arm, 8 SC, 4 SC together with the arm, 4 SC (24).</li><li><strong>17.</strong> 24 SC.</li><li><strong>18.</strong> Back loops only: (2 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>19.</strong> 18 SC.</li></ul><p>Fasten off and cut the thread. Add an edging of white fluffy yarn in rows 8 and 18 by crocheting 1 SC in each stitch.</p><h2>Hat</h2><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in magic ring.</li><li><strong>2–4.</strong> 6 SC each.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 3 (9).</li><li><strong>6–8.</strong> 9 SC each.</li><li><strong>9.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 3 (12).</li><li><strong>10–12.</strong> 12 SC each.</li><li><strong>13.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 3 (15).</li><li><strong>14–16.</strong> 15 SC each.</li><li><strong>17.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 3 (18).</li><li><strong>18–19.</strong> 18 SC each.</li><li><strong>20.</strong> (5 SC, inc) x 3 (21).</li><li><strong>21.</strong> 21 SC.</li><li><strong>22.</strong> (6 SC, inc) x 3 (24).</li><li><strong>23.</strong> (7 SC, inc) x 3 (27).</li><li><strong>24.</strong> (8 SC, inc) x 3 (30).</li><li><strong>25.</strong> 30 SC.</li><li><strong>26.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>27.</strong> 36 SC.</li><li><strong>28.</strong> (5 SC, inc) x 6 (42).</li><li><strong>29.</strong> 42 SC.</li><li><strong>30.</strong> (6 SC, inc) x 6 (48).</li><li><strong>31–32.</strong> 48 SC each.</li><li><strong>33.</strong> (7 SC, inc) x 6 (54).</li><li><strong>34–35.</strong> 54 SC each.</li></ul><p>In the front loops of row 35, work an edging with white fluffy yarn by working 1 SC in each stitch.</p><h2>Assembly / Decoration</h2><ul><li>Embroider the nose, eyebrows, and smile using dark green thread.</li><li>Embroider the eyelashes with black thread.</li></ul>`,
