    title: "Spider Kitty Crochet Pattern Amigurumi Cat in Hero Costume with Ears Hat",
    description: "Crochet a 20 cm kitty dressed in a red-and-blue hero costume, with a cat-ear hat. The white head, red mittens and blue sleeves and legs make a cute color-blocked toy. He’s a fun handmade gift or a great Halloween project.",
    author: "crochet art",
    patternText: `<h2>Abbreviations</h2><ul><li><strong>SC:</strong> single crochet</li><li><strong>MR:</strong> magic ring</li><li><strong>Inc:</strong> increase</li><li><strong>Sl St:</strong> slip stitch</li><li><strong>Ch:</strong> chain</li><li><strong>Dec:</strong> decrease</li></ul><h2>Materials</h2><ul><li>Milk cotton yarn (white, red, blue)</li><li>10 mm safety eyes</li><li>4 mm crochet hook</li><li>Thin yellow and black threads</li><li>Toy stuffing</li><li>Felting wool or thin embroidery thread for details</li><li><strong>Finished toy size:</strong> 20 cm</li></ul><h2>Arms (Make 2)</h2><p><em>Start with red yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3–4.</strong> 12 SC (2 rows).</li></ul><p><em>Switch to blue yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>5–9.</strong> 12 SC (5 rows).</li><li><strong>10.</strong> (1 SC, dec) x 4 (8).</li></ul><p>Fold in half and crochet 4 SC across both sides.</p><h2>Head</h2><p><em>Work with white yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>7.</strong> (5 SC, inc) x 6 (42).</li><li><strong>8–12.</strong> 42 SC (5 rows).</li><li><strong>13.</strong> (5 SC, dec) x 6 (36).</li><li><strong>14.</strong> (4 SC, dec) x 6 (30).</li><li><strong>15.</strong> (3 SC, dec) x 6 (24).</li><li><strong>16.</strong> (2 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>17.</strong> (1 SC, dec) x 6 (12).</li><li><strong>18.</strong> 6 dec.</li></ul><p>Insert the eyes between rows 10–11 at a distance of 8 SC.</p><h2>Ears</h2><p>Make 2 white ears for the cat head and 2 red ears for the hat:</p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 4 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 2 (6).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 2 (8).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 2 (10).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 2 (12).</li></ul><p>Sew the white ears onto the head from the 3rd to 8th row, leaving a 5–6 SC distance from the eyes.</p><h2>Hat</h2><p><em>Work with red yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 7 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 7 inc (14).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 7 (21).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> (2 SC, inc) x 7 (28).</li><li><strong>5.</strong> (3 SC, inc) x 7 (35).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> (4 SC, inc) x 7 (42).</li><li><strong>7–13.</strong> 42 SC (7 rows).</li></ul><p>Sew the red ears onto the hat slightly closer to the front (when folded in half) on rows 5–9.</p><h2>Legs and Body</h2><p><em>Start with red yarn for the legs:</em></p><ul><li><strong>1.</strong> 6 SC in MR.</li><li><strong>2.</strong> 6 inc (12).</li><li><strong>3.</strong> (1 SC, inc) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>4.</strong> 18 SC.</li><li><strong>5.</strong> 4 SC, 4 dec, 6 SC (14).</li><li><strong>6.</strong> 5 SC, 2 dec, 5 SC (12).</li><li><strong>7–8.</strong> 12 SC (2 rows).</li></ul><p>On the 8th row, close using blue yarn for a smooth transition.</p><p><em>Switch to blue yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>9–13.</strong> 12 SC (5 rows).</li></ul><p>On the second leg, leave 1–2 SC unworked if needed to align the legs straight. Make 2 chains and connect to the first leg.</p><ul><li><strong>14.</strong> 28 SC and place marker.</li><li><strong>15.</strong> 28 SC (close the top with red for a smooth transition).</li></ul><p><em>Switch to red yarn:</em></p><ul><li><strong>16–18.</strong> 28 SC (3 rows).</li><li><strong>18–20.</strong> 4 SC, 19 SC, 5 SC (3 rows).</li><li><strong>21.</strong> 4 SC, 2 SC, dec, 11 SC, dec, 2 SC, 5 SC (26).</li><li><strong>22.</strong> 2 SC, dec, 17 SC, dec, 3 SC (24).</li><li><strong>23.</strong> 3 SC, 4 SC (together with arm), 9 SC, 4 SC (together with arm), 4 SC (24).</li><li><strong>24.</strong> (2 SC, dec) x 6 (18).</li><li><strong>25.</strong> (1 SC, dec) x 6 (12).</li><li><strong>26.</strong> 12 SC in any color.</li></ul>`,
